# Everything under build/ is derived from the song's inputs and is rebuilt by
# `./infra/run.sh <song> fetch align`. Nothing in here is worth a history:
# the downloaded audio, the extracted MusicXML, the engraved rows, the sync map.
build/

# The rendered video. One filename per song, overwritten on every render --
# exactly the kind of large binary that git is worst at storing.
*_playalong.mkv

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# reloj's media: the source video, a re-encode of it, and the backing audio.
# All three are downloads, not inputs -- song.json names the recording they come
# from. The source is the play-along already published on the author's own
# channel -- the one URL nobody else can take down -- and its audio is the same
# backing track from the same first sample (verified: zero lag), followed by the
# silence the render appends. Keeping these would be 18 MB of history for files
# that a URL already describes.
reloj/reloj_video_hd.webm
reloj/reloj_video_small.mp4
reloj/reloj_backing.webm

# The photo of the sheet reloj was transcribed from. A reference, not an input:
# the notes it holds are in reloj.mxl, and nothing here reads the image.
reloj/partitura_original.png

# MuseScore's own project file. The pipeline reads only the .mxl, and the
# editable score lives in MuseScore's cloud -- see score_source in song.json.
# Keeping a second copy here would be the mirror this repo deliberately avoids.
reloj/reloj.mscz
